  "instructions": "Read every relevant eligible journey in the supplied prepared Results evidence. Return a short JSON list of decision-changing comparisons with exact J aliases. Look across cabin choices, especially equal-schedule economy/business options, and distinguish same schedule from identical flight or booking facts. Check full arrival dates and points programs. Do not select an exclusive shortlist or author prose.\n\nExact-choice reading guide: each journey group's facts give the whole-journey route, full dated departure/arrival, duration, cabin and booking obligation for every member in that group. Each member's choice.award_quote and choice.cash_quote copy only its exact referenced component's reported facts; state=unknown or absent and unknown price_scope remain unknown. Never move a quote, cabin, seat or booking fact between J members. reasons_ref, cost_ref, assessments_ref and positioning_reason_ref are zero-based indexes into the same-named journey_fact_catalog arrays; use each full indexed value as the group fact. same_schedule lists all J members by matching reported route, full timestamps, duration and transfer facts. An unknown schedule is listed alone and proves no timing relationship; matching does not prove the same physical flights, price, cabin, booking or availability. Compare cabins and arrival timing separately across meaningful alternatives, especially an economy option matching a business option's schedule. Do not assume a schedule improvement is purchased by a cabin upgrade when an eligible same-schedule economy choice exists.\n\nFor each J alias, choice.identity repeats that exact member's full dated journey route, schedule, duration, cabin and booking obligation. choice.award_quote.carriers and cabin are reported component facts; the points program is not a flight carrier. choice.traveler_seat_assessment lists that journey's traveler and minimum-seat reason states. Interpret these separately from price_scope and preserve unknown evidence.\nEach refs array item must be one existing exact J, A or C alias, or an existing comparison-pool alias only when it maps to the entire eligible journey pool. Do not use ranges (such as J1–J232), comma-joined aliases, or prose in refs. P1 describes the whole eligible pool, never a separate-ticket subset. For a subset, enumerate exact aliases or name clearly scoped examples in finding without claiming exhaustive coverage. Do not invent or expand aliases.\n",
